@server=http://localhost:4004
@agent=/a2a/hr-agent

# `npm run hybrid` (cds watch --profile hybrid) runs the agent locally against
# the real model: AI Core through the AICORE_DESTINATION destination. This is
# the only way to see the agent reason and pick its tools — the local
# profile's `llm-mock` never calls one.
#
# Logins are the mocked users from package.json (alice, bob, carol; empty
# password). The conversation below is the one the agent is built for.


### Agent card
# @name agent_card
GET {{server}}{{agent}}/.well-known/agent-card.json
Authorization: Basic alice:


### 1. Ask for a leave in one sentence
# Watch the server log: the model should call `planAnnualLeave` with
# startDay 10, startMonth 11, workingDays 3 and no year, and answer with the
# plan instead of filing it. Filing straight away, or asking for the year, is
# the first sign that AGENTS.md or the tool descriptions need work.
# @name plan
POST {{server}}{{agent}}/
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic alice:

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": "1",
  "method": "message/send",
  "params": {
    "message": {
      "kind": "message",
      "messageId": "msg-1",
      "role": "user",
      "parts": [
        { "kind": "text", "text": "I'd like to take 3 days of annual leave starting 10 November, can you plan it?" }
      ]
    }
  }
}


### 2. Agree to the plan
# The model should now call `submitAnnualLeave`. Because the action carries
# `@agent.hitl`, the task stops in `input-required` with an approval request
# instead of completing.
# @name agree
POST {{server}}{{agent}}/
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic alice:

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": "2",
  "method": "message/send",
  "params": {
    "message": {
      "kind": "message",
      "messageId": "msg-2",
      "role": "user",
      "contextId": "{{plan.response.body.result.contextId}}",
      "parts": [
        { "kind": "text", "text": "Yes, please file it." }
      ]
    }
  }
}


### 3. Approve the tool call
# Answering the paused task with "approve" lets `submitAnnualLeave` run. The
# reply should carry the request number and a link to the PDF.
# @name approve
POST {{server}}{{agent}}/
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic alice:

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": "3",
  "method": "message/send",
  "params": {
    "message": {
      "kind": "message",
      "messageId": "msg-3",
      "role": "user",
      "contextId": "{{plan.response.body.result.contextId}}",
      "taskId": "{{agree.response.body.result.id}}",
      "parts": [
        { "kind": "text", "text": "approve" }
      ]
    }
  }
}


### Ask for something out of scope
# AGENTS.md says to name the limit: sick leave is handled by HR directly.
POST {{server}}{{agent}}/
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic alice:

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": "4",
  "method": "message/send",
  "params": {
    "message": {
      "kind": "message",
      "messageId": "msg-4",
      "role": "user",
      "parts": [
        { "kind": "text", "text": "I'm sick tomorrow and will get a doctor's note. Can you enter sick leave?" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
